    {
      "type": "Block",
      "value": "---\nesid: sec-Intl.Locale.prototype.getCalendars\ndescription: >\n  The region used to look up the calendar preference is chosen from the\n  available signals in the correct priority order.\ninfo: |\n  CalendarsOfLocale ( loc )\n  ...\n  2. Let _preference_ be RegionPreference(_loc_.[[Locale]]).\n  3. Let _region_ be _preference_.[[Region]].\n  4. Let _regionOverride_ be _preference_.[[RegionOverride]].\n  5. If _regionOverride_ is not *undefined* and calendar preference data for\n     _regionOverride_ are available, then\n    a. Let _lookupRegion_ be _regionOverride_.\n  6. Else,\n    a. Let _lookupRegion_ be _region_.\n  ...\n\n  RegionPreference ( locale )\n  1. Let _region_ be GetLocaleRegion(_locale_).\n  2. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n    a. Set _region_ to CanonicalUnicodeSubdivision(_locale_, *\"sd\"*).\n    b. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n      i. Let _maximal_ be the result of the Add Likely Subtags algorithm applied\n         to _locale_. If an error is signaled, set _maximal_ to _locale_.\n      ii. Set _maximal_ to CanonicalizeUnicodeLocaleId(_maximal_).\n      iii. Set _region_ to GetLocaleRegion(_maximal_).\n      iv. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n        1. Set _region_ to *\"001\"*.\n  3. Let _regionOverride_ be CanonicalUnicodeSubdivision(_locale_, *\"rg\"*).\n  4. Return { [[Region]]: _region_, [[RegionOverride]]: _regionOverride_ }.\nfeatures: [Intl.Locale, Intl.Locale-info]\n---",
      "start": 124,
      "end": 1528
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Together, CalendarsOfLocale and RegionPreference select the region used to",
      "start": 1530,
      "end": 1607
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " look up the calendar preference from the available signals in this priority",
      "start": 1608,
      "end": 1686
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " order (highest first):",
      "start": 1687,
      "end": 1712
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 1713,
      "end": 1715
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   1. the \"rg\" region override keyword (when calendar data for it exists)",
      "start": 1716,
      "end": 1791
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   2. the region subtag",
      "start": 1792,
      "end": 1817
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   3. the \"sd\" subdivision keyword",
      "start": 1818,
      "end": 1854
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   4. the region computed by the Add Likely Subtags algorithm",
      "start": 1855,
      "end": 1918
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   5. the \"001\" (world) region",
      "start": 1919,
      "end": 1951
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 1952,
      "end": 1954
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Each entry below is a locale that carries the signal for its priority level",
      "start": 1955,
      "end": 2033
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " on top of all lower-priority signals, paired with a locale that names the",
      "start": 2034,
      "end": 2110
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " region that signal must resolve to. The paired locale uses the same base",
      "start": 2111,
      "end": 2186
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " language so that any language-dependent locale data is held constant. For",
      "start": 2187,
      "end": 2263
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " example, \"fa-JP-u-sd-inka-rg-thzzzz\" carries an \"rg\" override of region \"TH\",",
      "start": 2264,
      "end": 2344
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " a region subtag \"JP\", an \"sd\" subdivision in region \"IN\", and a base language",
      "start": 2345,
      "end": 2425
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " \"fa\" whose likely region is \"IR\"; the \"rg\" override has the highest priority,",
      "start": 2426,
      "end": 2506
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " so the locale must behave like \"fa-TH\".",
      "start": 2507,
      "end": 2549
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 2550,
      "end": 2552
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " The last entry has no lower-priority signals: the language \"eo\" (Esperanto)",
      "start": 2553,
      "end": 2631
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " has no likely region, so its region falls back to \"001\".",
      "start": 2632,
      "end": 2691
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " For each priority level to be observable, the region it selects must have",
      "start": 3136,
      "end": 3212
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " different calendars than the region selected by the next lower level in this",
      "start": 3213,
      "end": 3292
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " implementation; otherwise the test could not tell them apart.",
      "start": 3293,
      "end": 3357
    }
  ],
